.TH MOXY-RENDER 1 "" "moxy"
.SH NAME
moxy-render \- Render or reverse-resolve a namespaced tool/prompt name under a template
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moxy render
.RI [ --name-template = STRING ]
.RI [ --server = STRING ]
.RI [ --tool = STRING ]
.RI [ --resolve = STRING ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Forward (default): prints the advertised name for --server/--tool under --name-template. Reverse (--resolve <rendered>): prints the canonical "server<TAB>tool" via a structural inverse, which works only for invertible templates (exactly one {server} and one {tool} separated by a literal). render does NOT introspect a running server — pass the same --name-template you gave serve-http. See docs/features/0007-name-template.md.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --name-template
Template using {server} and {tool}. Default '{server}.{tool}'.
Default: 
.TP
.B --server
Server name (forward direction).
Default: 
.TP
.B --tool
Tool or prompt name (forward direction).
Default: 
.TP
.B --resolve
Reverse-resolve this rendered name to 'server<TAB>tool' instead of rendering forward.
Default: 
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moxy (1)
